{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the main narrative of Section 5 (RCE Deep Dive) #}
{# NOTE: The original REPORT_STRUCTURE incorrectly had section3_narrative.j2 here. This should be section5_narrative.j2 #}
{% set output_format_description = "a coherent narrative paragraph (or potentially two short paragraphs) summarizing the analysis of RCE vulnerabilities, suitable for the main body text. Use Markdown for clarity (e.g., simple bolding) if helpful." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Synthesize the provided chart insights, callouts, and data summaries for "{{ section_title }}" into a flowing narrative text focused specifically on Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerabilities.
Your narrative should cover:
1. The trend in the proportion of RCE vulnerabilities relative to all CVEs during the reporting period.
2. The typical severity profile of these RCE vulnerabilities based on their CVSS score distribution.
Integrate the key points highlighted in the callouts regarding the significance of RCEs. Aim for 3-6 sentences. You may use simple Markdown (like **bold**) for emphasis if appropriate.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Section Key: {{ data_context_payload.section_key | default('section_5_rce_deep_dive') }}

Chart Insights Generated for this Section:
{% for chart_id, insight in data_context_payload.chart_insights_in_section.items() %}
- Insight ({{ chart_id }}): {{ insight }}
{% else %}
- No specific chart insights provided.
{% endfor %}

Callouts Generated for this Section:
{% for callout_key, callout_text in data_context_payload.callouts_in_section.items() %}
- {{ callout_key | replace("_", " ") | title }}: {{ callout_text }}
{% else %}
- No callouts generated for this section.
{% endfor %}

Data Summaries for Charts in this Section:
{% for chart_id, summary in data_context_payload.charts_data_summaries_in_section.items() %}
--- Data Summary: {{ chart_id }} ---
{{ summary }}
--- End Summary ---
{% else %}
- No chart data summaries provided.
{% endfor %}
{% endblock data_context %}
